chapter.v:
I repeat, 


let no, 


one think me foolish. But even if you do, accept me as a fool, so that I too may boast a little.

Three times 


I was, 


beaten with rods. Once I was stoned. Three times I was shipwrecked; a night and a day I was adrift at sea;

on frequent 


journeys, in, 


danger from rivers, danger from robbers, danger from my own people, danger from Gentiles, danger in the city, danger in the wilderness, danger at sea, danger from false brothers;

And, apart 


from other, 


things, there is the daily pressure on me of my anxiety for all the churches.
